 "script": {
  "hook": "Three lines will get you through any konbini checkout, even on your first day in Japan.",
  "points": [
   "First, you are holding a bento at the counter. The clerk asks, あたためますか. That is, shall I heat it up? Say, おねがいします. You are saying, yes, please.",
   "Second, the bag. The clerk asks, ふくろは、いりますか. That is, do you want a bag? To say no thanks, say, だいじょうぶです. You are saying, I am fine.",
   "Third, the chopsticks. The clerk asks, おはしを、おつけしますか. That is, shall I add chopsticks? To pass, say, いらないです. You are saying, I do not need them."
  ],
  "takeaway": "Quick extra. If the clerk forgets to ask, you can lead. Say, あたためてください. In English, please heat this. Say all three out loud once before your next trip.",
  "cta": "Save this for your next trip to Japan."
 },
